tier: 1
face: query
expect: ok
note: A "__proto__" rule key parses (JSON.parse defines it as an OWN property, so it is in the
note: parsed tree) but cannot be written: extractAt does `result[key] =`, which on a plain object
note: hits the legacy Object.prototype __proto__ setter and re-parents `result` instead of adding
note: a key. The key is silently absent from the output; sibling keys are unaffected.
